    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"short_to_ground\",\n      \"components\": [\"J12\", \"U1\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"J12.A6\", \"J12.B6\", \"U1.27\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"GND\", \"/Microcontroller/USB_D+\"],\n      \"observed\": \"Both USB-C D+ contacts on J12 (A6 and B6) and the ESP32-C3 GPIO19/USB_D+ pin (U1.27) are listed on the GND net. The USB D+ net that should exist between them is absent. Its partner, USB_D- (net /Microcontroller/USB_D-), is correctly wired to J12 A7/B7 and U1.26.\",\n      \"expected\": \"USB D+ (J12 A6/B6 and U1 pin 27 GPIO19/USB_D+) should form a separate differential-pair net, paired with USB D- on J12 A7/B7 and U1 pin 26. It should not be tied to ground.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"12\\\") (name \\\"GND\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"J12\\\") (pin \\\"A6\\\") (pinfunction \\\"D+\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\")) ... (node (ref \\\"J12\\\") (pin \\\"B6\\\") (pinfunction \\\"D+\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\")) ... (node (ref \\\"U1\\\") (pin \\\"27\\\") (pinfunction \\\"GPIO19/USB_D+\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"6\\\") (name \\\"/Microcontroller/USB_D-\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"J12\\\") (pin \\\"A7\\\") (pinfunction \\\"D-\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"U1\\\") (pin \\\"26\\\") (pinfunction \\\"GPIO18/USB_D-\\\")\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"USB D+ is hard-shorted to ground, so the ESP32's native USB interface cannot enumerate or communicate. Firmware flashing and USB serial debugging over the USB-C port would fail, and the D+ driver could be damaged.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.9\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist places the USB D+ pins (J12 A6/B6 and ESP32 U1 pin 27/GPIO19) on the GND net, shorting the USB data line to ground while D- is correctly routed. The rest of the power, heater, thermocouple and passive wiring matches the specification, and the reverse-biased D7 and fixed-value parts are documented in the spec, so this USB short is the single clear anomaly.\"\n}",
